WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.637
Why does this gate need code?

2
00:00:01.637 --> 00:00:05.232
The guide's Gate 5 ties the
card's lifecycle to the person's:

3
00:00:05.232 --> 00:00:09.287
the card is issued from a joiner
record and revoked from a leaver.

4
00:00:09.287 --> 00:00:13.137
But revocation only reaches
sign-in through the CRL,

5
00:00:13.137 --> 00:00:15.912
and a CRL grows with every revocation.

6
00:00:15.912 --> 00:00:20.712
The day it crosses the limit is the day
sign-in fails for every card from that CA.

7
00:00:20.712 --> 00:00:22.537
So the check runs every day.

8
00:00:22.537 --> 00:00:25.686
Per-user binding coverage is
the validation kit's job;

9
00:00:25.686 --> 00:00:29.830
this chapter checks the tenant's
settings, which that kit doesn't read.
